## I also want to evolve the idea

I would make it broader than construction.

# Name

**Pulse**

> *The Operating System for Field Operations.*

Not construction software.

Not ERP.

A cloud-native operations platform for organizations whose employees work **outside the office**.

Industries:

* Construction
* HVAC
* Electrical
* Plumbing
* Solar
* Telecom
* Utilities
* Facility Management
* Landscaping
* Mining
* Agriculture
* Oil & Gas
* Road Maintenance
* Government Public Works
* Inspection Services
* Equipment Rental

Construction becomes **the first vertical**, but the architecture is built to support all field-service industries.

That positioning makes the project much more impressive because the domain model is generalized instead of hardcoded around construction.

## I strongly recommend building this documentation as a book

Rather than a single massive prompt, we'll produce a cohesive specification where each chapter builds on the previous one.

The end result will be something you can hand to Antigravity IDE and say:

> "Build this."

And it will have enough context to generate production-quality architecture instead of disconnected CRUD code.

**I believe this could become one of the strongest portfolio projects I've seen** because it demonstrates product thinking, enterprise architecture, cloud engineering, DevOps, and practical AI engineering in a single platform.
